    "oct_p4": "<strong>Ten languages</strong>, a load forecast and smarter daily briefings.",
    "oct_p3": "<strong>Polar Flow:</strong> import your activities and send planned workouts to your watch.",
    "oct_p2": "<strong>Workout fuel:</strong> carbs, fluids and sodium for each session, and a quick log of what you actually took.",
    "oct_p1": "<strong>Strength training:</strong> programmes built around your race goals, with a gym mode for sets, reps and loads.",
    "oct_summary": "October turned Fjelia into a training partner: strength workouts with a gym mode, a fuel plan for every session, Polar sync, and an app that speaks your language.",
    "nov_summary": "<p>In November, your training history comes with you to Fjelia: import your Strava ZIP archive directly on your iPhone, including activities, recorded routes and any photos or videos it contains. The importer recognizes existing sessions and adds missing photos. You can also import individual FIT, GPX and TCX files.</p><p>You can rename activities in Fjelia, add your own pictures and share them as styled cards. Deleted sessions no longer reappear after the next sync; you can restore them under “Recently deleted”. When you ask about a workout, the AI coach also considers your plan and the sessions before and after it.</p><p>COROS workouts now include routes and heart-rate graphs. Importing sleep, HRV and stress data has also improved. A new overview brings together your LT1, LT2 and FTP training thresholds. Other additions include waist-measurement history, DWD weather forecasts and short-term rain forecasts for planning your training in Germany.</p>",
